You recall the canister with herbicide, taken from the shed. It's time to find out, if it is fit for something except extermination of weed.
Trying not to make abrupt movements, you carefully take the canister, remove the stopper and shower the branch adhered to Irene with chemical liquid. The fuzz covered with shining drops, begin to turn dark and shrink before your eyes, but the stubborn plant keeps holding the girl. Irene starts to cry.
"Wait, now it will take effect" you try to calm her down, being not so sure about success too.
Quite a lot of time has passed, before the substance finally kills sticky fuzz, adhered to Irene's arm. You take her very carefully by the shoulders; pull her out of the plant. Both of you fall powerlessly on the grass, gasping for air. Irene is embracing you tightly, shaking in sobbing. So you sit on the ground, holding each other, trying not to think about a gruesome fate, that you miraculously managed to escape.
Having recovered yourselves, you go back. Now it is clear, that the path through the lilac plants is deadly dangerous, so you have no other option, but to make your way through the thick shrubs of white flower bushes.